8,8,8,8,8],[1,1,8,4,8,1,1,8,1,8,8,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,1],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,1],[8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,1,8,1,1,8,4,8,1,1,8,8,8,8,1,1,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,1,8,1,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,1,8,1,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,1,8],[1,1,8,8,8,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,1,8,4,8,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,1,8,8,8],[8,8,8,1,8,8,1,1,8,8,1,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,8],[1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,1,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,1,1,8,8,8,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,1,1,8,8,8,8,8,1,8]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"The grid is plain background (8) with many 1-coloured dominoes. Only a few background cells turn to 4, and those cells always sit in a specific spot.\n\n**Looking at the changed cells**\n\n- **Pair 2, cell (4,3):**\n  - Above it, the vertical domino (1,3)-(2,3) is separated from it by the empty cell (3,3).\n  - Below it, the vertical domino (6,3)-(7,3) is separated by (5,3).\n  - To the left, the horizontal domino (4,0)-(4,1) is separated by (4,2).\n  - To the right, the horizontal domino (4,5)-(4,6) is separated by (4,4).\n- **Pair 1, cell (5,4):** the same picture.\n  - Vertical dominoes are at rows 2–3 and 7–8 in column 4.\n  - Horizontal dominoes are at columns 1–2 and 6–7 in row 5.\n- **Pair 3, cells (5,10) and (11,12):** each one has this complete four-armed \"cross\" of dominoes.\n\nOther dominoes in the grids form only partial crosses, and their centres stay unchanged.\n\n**Rule**\n\nA background cell becomes 4 when all of the following hold:\n- the cells at offsets 2 and 3 straight up are both 1;\n- the cells at offsets 2 and 3 straight down are both 1;\n- the cells at offsets 2 and 3 straight left are both 1;\n- the cells at offsets 2 and 3 straight right are both 1.\n\nSo the four dominoes point toward the cell, each with a one-cell gap. Cells closer than 3 to an edge cannot qualify.\n\nThe domino colour is taken as the non-background colour actually present, and the background is computed from the grid. The marker colour 4 is the same in every pair, so it is a constant.\n\n**On the test (20×20)**\n\nThe program scans every cell with the same check and marks each centre of a complete cross. It emits one stage per marked centre, then emits the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    fg = [c for c in np.unique(g) if c != bg]\n    if not fg:\n        emit(out, \"No foreground dominoes; nothing to mark.\")\n        return out\n    fc = fg[0]\n    for y in range(H):\n        for x in range(W):\n            if g[y, x] != bg:\n                continue\n            ok = True\n            for dy, dx in ((-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)):\n                for k in (2, 3):\n                    yy, xx = y + dy * k, x + dx * k\n                    if not (0 <= yy < H and 0 <= xx < W) or g[yy, xx] != fc:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    break\n            if ok:\n                out[y, x] = 4\n                emit(out, f\"Cell ({y},{x}) is surrounded by four dominoes (up, down, left, right, each one gap away): mark it 4.\")\n    emit(out, \"All cross centres marked.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"96dd65ef2eee2d551a9abc101f2b1ac57c9c25e8d30889d2fc54c8f0a3d0b6cf","task_sha256":"e847d2d3fe02036f1bbeb02a36c273e7e2ed8682b82eb515d77f4e57d60985d4","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
